{"componentChunkName":"component---src-components-module-blog-post-index-jsx","path":"/posts/git-autocompletion/","result":{"data":{"site":{"siteMetadata":{"author":"Gokul prabhu","siteUrl":"https://codefromdude.com"}},"post":{"html":"<img src=\"/assets/blog/git-autocompletion/git-autocompletion.gif\" alt=\"git auto completion\" style=\"width:100%\">\n<p>Remembering the branches and all the available commands are daunting work in git. what if the commands auto-completes itself like shown in the above gif. we can save a lot of typing. not all of us have a typing speed of 90+ wpm right?.</p>\n<p>For this, we need to configure our terminal with git auto-completion snippet. you can download the bash-completion file from <a href=\"https://github.com/git/git/tree/master/contrib/completion\">here</a>.\nDownload the file from these links if you're using <a href=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/master/contrib/completion/git-completion.bash\">bash</a>, or <a href=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/master/contrib/completion/git-completion.zsh\">zsh</a> or <a href=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/master/contrib/completion/git-prompt.sh\">shell</a>.</p>\n<p>You can download with simple curl command also like this,</p>\n\n          <div class=\"gatsby-remark-prismjs-copy-button-container\">\n            <div class=\"gatsby-remark-prismjs-copy-button\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\" aria-pressed=\"false\" onclick=\"gatsbyRemarkCopyToClipboard(this, this.parentNode.nextElementSibling)\">\n              Copy\n            </div>\n          </div>\n          \n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"bash\"><pre class=\"language-bash\"><code class=\"language-bash\"><span class=\"token function\">curl</span> https://raw.githubusercontent.com/git/git/master/contrib/completion/git-completion.bash <span class=\"token parameter variable\">-o</span> ~/.git-completion.bash</code></pre></div>\n<p>and add the downloaded file in <em>~/.bashrc</em> or <em>~/.zshrc</em> depends on your terminal like this.</p>\n\n          <div class=\"gatsby-remark-prismjs-copy-button-container\">\n            <div class=\"gatsby-remark-prismjs-copy-button\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\" aria-pressed=\"false\" onclick=\"gatsbyRemarkCopyToClipboard(this, this.parentNode.nextElementSibling)\">\n              Copy\n            </div>\n          </div>\n          \n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"bash\"><pre class=\"language-bash\"><code class=\"language-bash\"><span class=\"token comment\"># bash</span>\n<span class=\"token keyword\">if</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">[</span> <span class=\"token parameter variable\">-f</span> ~/.git-completion.bash <span class=\"token punctuation\">]</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">then</span>\n  <span class=\"token builtin class-name\">.</span> ~/.git-completion.bash\n<span class=\"token keyword\">fi</span></code></pre></div>\n\n          <div class=\"gatsby-remark-prismjs-copy-button-container\">\n            <div class=\"gatsby-remark-prismjs-copy-button\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\" aria-pressed=\"false\" onclick=\"gatsbyRemarkCopyToClipboard(this, this.parentNode.nextElementSibling)\">\n              Copy\n            </div>\n          </div>\n          \n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"bash\"><pre class=\"language-bash\"><code class=\"language-bash\"><span class=\"token comment\">#zsh</span>\n<span class=\"token builtin class-name\">source</span> ~/.git-completion.bash</code></pre></div>\n<p>restart the terminal and enjoy the git auto-completion.</p>","excerpt":"Remembering the branches and all the available commands are daunting work in git. what if the commands auto-completes itself like shown in…","timeToRead":1,"tableOfContents":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Git autocompletion","path":"git-autocompletion","tags":["git","cmdline"],"date":"2020-11-08T12:30:34.813Z","parentPath":null}},"parentPost":null,"siblingPosts":{"edges":[]},"previousPost":{"frontmatter":{"title":"You tried hard and you gave your best! still you failed and it's ok!"}},"nextPost":{"frontmatter":{"title":"Evaluating documentation frameworks for personal projects."}}},"pageContext":{"parentPath":null,"relatedPosts":[{"title":"A missing cmdline util for GIT - NIT","path":"git-cmdline-util","date":"2020-01-18T07:52:06.942Z"},{"title":"Local aliases using zen aliases","path":"zen-alias","date":"2021-02-05T19:22:59.656Z"},{"title":"Better cmdline","path":"better-cmdline-1","date":"2019-06-09T12:25:19.116Z"}],"pageId":"a16ad469-4304-5d24-9238-dda73912015a","previousPagePath":"/posts/you-tried-hard-and-failed-its-ok/","previousItem":{"node":{"id":"f3fbe7c2-bbbe-5137-a46b-72445c48600a","frontmatter":{"title":"You tried hard and you gave your best! still you failed and it's ok!","path":"you-tried-hard-and-failed-its-ok","parentPath":null,"date":"2020-11-20T03:41:38.083Z","categories":["personal"],"tags":["personal","motivation","outliers"]}},"context":{"parentPath":null,"relatedPosts":[]}},"previousPageId":"f3fbe7c2-bbbe-5137-a46b-72445c48600a","nextPagePath":"/posts/eval-documentation-frameworks-for-personal-projects/","nextItem":{"node":{"id":"1ea5dbea-02de-5a6b-bbbf-03664fe2cf1b","frontmatter":{"title":"Evaluating documentation frameworks for personal projects.","path":"eval-documentation-frameworks-for-personal-projects","parentPath":null,"date":"2020-05-03T06:10:35.547Z","categories":["programming"],"tags":["documentation","gitbook","mkdocs","docsify","gitdocs","daux","docusaurus"]}},"context":{"parentPath":null,"relatedPosts":[{"title":"Top 10 tools you need as developer","path":"top-10-tools-you-need-as-dev","date":"2023-03-11T13:07:07.000Z"},{"title":"mhowls (Must have or we look stupid)","path":"til-mhowls","date":"2023-01-27T10:34:41.000Z"},{"title":"Being a privileged website","path":"being-a-privileged-website","date":"2022-10-17T09:03:29.000Z"}]}},"nextPageId":"1ea5dbea-02de-5a6b-bbbf-03664fe2cf1b"}},"staticQueryHashes":["983108779"],"slicesMap":{}}